<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<LanguageData>
  <!--EN: Build large wooden pyres, that when lit on fire are guaranteed to summon friendly reinforcements.-->
  <VFEC_Beacons.description>建造大型木柴堆，点燃时一定会召唤友军增援。</VFEC_Beacons.description>
  <VFEC_Beacons.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->pyres of summoning-->
    <li>subject-&gt;召唤火堆</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->constructed large wooden pyres, a signal to the skies that calls forth allies to the battlefield-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;建造了大型木柴堆，向天空发出信号，召唤盟友前往战场</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->binding the fates of allies with flames that guide them to the fray-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;用火焰束缚盟友的命运，引导他们投入战斗</li>
  </VFEC_Beacons.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: beacons-->
  <VFEC_Beacons.label>信标</VFEC_Beacons.label>
  <!--EN: Mix steel with stone chunks to create slightly weaker metal in large quantities.-->
  <VFEC_BronzeWorking.description>将钢与石块混合以大量制造稍弱的金属。</VFEC_BronzeWorking.description>
  <VFEC_BronzeWorking.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the alloy of antiquity-->
    <li>subject-&gt;古代合金</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->discovered the alchemy of combining steel with stone to produce bronze, marking the dawn of a new era in metallurgy-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;发现了钢石结合炼铜的炼金术，标志着冶金新时代的到来</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->ushering in an age where metal becomes the backbone of progress and power-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;迎来金属成为进步和力量支柱的时代</li>
  </VFEC_BronzeWorking.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: bronze working-->
  <VFEC_BronzeWorking.label>青铜加工</VFEC_BronzeWorking.label>
  <!--EN: Construct a cement press, which allows you to create extremely durable stone material out of stone chunks.-->
  <VFEC_CementMaking.description>建造一台水泥压机，用它可以用石块制造出极其耐用的石材。</VFEC_CementMaking.description>
  <VFEC_CementMaking.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the bedrock of civilization-->
    <li>subject-&gt;文明的基石</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->innovated the creation of cement, turning stone into the durable foundation upon which empires are built-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;创新了水泥的制造，将石头变成了建立帝国的持久基础</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->laying the groundwork for enduring structures and monuments with the strength of cement-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;利用水泥的强度为持久的结构和纪念碑奠定基础</li>
  </VFEC_CementMaking.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: cement making-->
  <VFEC_CementMaking.label>水泥制造</VFEC_CementMaking.label>
  <!--EN: Smith suits of centurion armor, excellent for leading men into heroic battles.-->
  <VFEC_CenturionArmor.description>史密斯穿着百夫长盔甲，非常适合带领士兵进行英勇的战斗。</VFEC_CenturionArmor.description>
  <VFEC_CenturionArmor.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->mantle of command-->
    <li>subject-&gt;指挥衣钵</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->smithed suits of centurion armor, imbuing leaders with both protection and a distinguished presence-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;精制的百夫长盔甲，为领导者提供保护和卓越的风采</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->clothing the ranks of leadership in armor befitting their valor and virtue-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;为领导层穿上与其英勇和美德相称的盔甲</li>
  </VFEC_CenturionArmor.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: centurion armor-->
  <VFEC_CenturionArmor.label>百夫长盔甲</VFEC_CenturionArmor.label>
  <!--EN: Build a workbench for crafting simple things like clubs or bows.-->
  <VFEC_CraftingBench.description>搭建一个工作台来制作简单的东西，例如球杆或弓。</VFEC_CraftingBench.description>
  <VFEC_CraftingBench.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the artisan's foundation-->
    <li>subject-&gt;工匠的基础</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->established crafting benches as the heart of production, where raw materials are transformed into tools and treasures-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;建立了作为生产核心的工艺台，原材料在这里被转化为工具和宝藏</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->carving the future with every crafted item, from the simplest club to the most precise bow-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;从最简单的球杆到最精确的弓，用每件精心制作的物品雕刻未来</li>
  </VFEC_CraftingBench.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: crafting bench-->
  <VFEC_CraftingBench.label>工艺台</VFEC_CraftingBench.label>
  <!--EN: Perform various plays on the theatre stage as a recreational activity.-->
  <VFEC_DramaAndComedy.description>在剧院舞台上表演各种戏剧作为一种娱乐活动。</VFEC_DramaAndComedy.description>
  <VFEC_DramaAndComedy.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the stage of life-->
    <li>subject-&gt;人生阶段</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->revived the timeless arts of drama and comedy, enriching the soul of the republic through performance and play-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;复兴了戏剧和喜剧的永恒艺术，通过表演和戏剧丰富了共和国的灵魂</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->mirroring the human condition, from tragedy to farce, on the communal stage-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;在公共舞台上反映从悲剧到闹剧的人类状况</li>
  </VFEC_DramaAndComedy.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: drama and comedy-->
  <VFEC_DramaAndComedy.label>drama and comedy</VFEC_DramaAndComedy.label>
  <!--EN: Create heavy scuta shields typically associated with legionnaires.-->
  <VFEC_HeavyShieldMaking.description>制造通常与军团士兵相关的重型盾牌。</VFEC_HeavyShieldMaking.description>
  <VFEC_HeavyShieldMaking.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->bulwarks of the legion-->
    <li>subject-&gt;军团的堡垒</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->reinvigorated the tradition of heavy shield crafting, providing unmatched protection to those who hold the line-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;重振了重型盾牌制作的传统，为坚守阵地的人们提供无与伦比的保护</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->forging the scuta shields, the steadfast guardians of the legionnaires-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;锻造盾牌，军团士兵的坚定守护者</li>
  </VFEC_HeavyShieldMaking.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: heavy shield making-->
  <VFEC_HeavyShieldMaking.label>重型盾牌制作</VFEC_HeavyShieldMaking.label>
  <!--EN: Craft tents, javelins, spathas and daggers, constituting towards the legionary armory.-->
  <VFEC_LegionaryArmaments.description>制作帐篷、标枪、斯帕塔和匕首，组成军团军械库。</VFEC_LegionaryArmaments.description>
  <VFEC_LegionaryArmaments.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->arsenal of the ancients-->
    <li>subject-&gt;古人的武器库</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->mastered the fabrication of javelins, spathas, and daggers, ensuring the legion's versatility and readiness in battle-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;掌握了标枪、斯帕塔和匕首的制造，确保了军团的多功能性和战备状态</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->equipping the legions with a diverse armory for conquest and defense-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;为军团配备多样化的军械库，用于征服和防御</li>
  </VFEC_LegionaryArmaments.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: legionary armaments-->
  <VFEC_LegionaryArmaments.label>军团武器</VFEC_LegionaryArmaments.label>
  <!--EN: Create heavy armor of legionaries, capable of withstanding a high degree of sharp damage.-->
  <VFEC_LegionnaireArmor.description>打造军团重甲，能够承受高度锐利伤害。</VFEC_LegionnaireArmor.description>
  <VFEC_LegionnaireArmor.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the iron skin-->
    <li>subject-&gt;铁皮</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->crafted heavy armor that turns warriors into indomitable forces on the battlefield, capable of withstanding the fiercest strikes-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;精心打造的重甲，让战士成为战场上不屈不挠的力量，能够承受最猛烈的打击</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->donning the legionnaires in armor that weaves invincibility with the threads of war-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;为军团士兵穿上盔甲，用战争的丝线编织出无敌的力量</li>
  </VFEC_LegionnaireArmor.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: legionary armor-->
  <VFEC_LegionnaireArmor.label>军团盔甲</VFEC_LegionnaireArmor.label>
  <!--EN: Construct meat drying racks, allowing you to preserve meat and create a roman delicacy.-->
  <VFEC_MeatDrying.description>建造肉类干燥架，让您保存肉类并创造罗马美食。</VFEC_MeatDrying.description>
  <VFEC_MeatDrying.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->legacy of preservation-->
    <li>subject-&gt;保护遗产</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->revived the ancient art of meat drying, securing sustenance and delighting palates with flavors honed by time-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;复兴了古老的肉类干燥艺术，确保了食物的安全，并用经过时间磨练的味道来愉悦味蕾</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->extending the bounty of the hunt through the wisdom of the ancients-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;通过古人的智慧扩大狩猎的范围</li>
  </VFEC_MeatDrying.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: meat drying-->
  <VFEC_MeatDrying.label>肉类干燥</VFEC_MeatDrying.label>
  <!--EN: Build excellent stone mosaics, utilising different colours and shapes to express beauty. Slow to construct.-->
  <VFEC_Mosaics.description>打造精美的石材马赛克，利用不同的颜色和形状来表达美感。建设缓慢。</VFEC_Mosaics.description>
  <VFEC_Mosaics.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->mosaic of civilization-->
    <li>subject-&gt;文明马赛克</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->crafted stone mosaics that capture the essence of beauty and narrative through color and form-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;精心制作的石材马赛克通过颜色和形式捕捉美感和叙事的本质</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->embedding the story of a people in the very stones that pave their path-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;将一个民族的故事嵌入到铺路的石头中</li>
  </VFEC_Mosaics.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: mosaics-->
  <VFEC_Mosaics.label>马赛克</VFEC_Mosaics.label>
  <!--EN: Construct paths, dirt roads and stone roads directly on the world map, allowing for faster caravan travel.-->
  <VFEC_RoadBuilding.description>直接在世界地图上建造道路、土路和石路，让商队旅行更快。</VFEC_RoadBuilding.description>
  <VFEC_RoadBuilding.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->pathways of progress-->
    <li>subject-&gt;进步之路</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->paved the way for civilization's expansion with the construction of roads, connecting communities and fostering trade-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;通过修建道路、连接社区和促进贸易为文明的扩展铺平道路</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->tracing the arteries of trade and communication with each road built, propelling the civilization forward-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;探寻每条道路的贸易和交流动脉，推动文明前进</li>
  </VFEC_RoadBuilding.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: road building-->
  <VFEC_RoadBuilding.label>道路建设</VFEC_RoadBuilding.label>
  <!--EN: Construct scorpions, a portable field artillery piece which doubles as a semi-automatic heavy crossbow.-->
  <VFEC_Scorpion.description>建造蝎子，一种便携式野战火炮，可兼作半自动重型十字弓。</VFEC_Scorpion.description>
  <VFEC_Scorpion.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->sting of the legion-->
    <li>subject-&gt;军团之刺</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->engineered scorpions, merging the precision of a crossbow with the destructive force of field artillery-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;工程蝎子，将十字弓的精准度与野战炮兵的破坏力融为一体</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->unleashing the lethal precision of ancient war machines upon the modern battlefield-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;在现代战场上释放古代战争机器的致命精度</li>
  </VFEC_Scorpion.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: scorpion-->
  <VFEC_Scorpion.label>蝎</VFEC_Scorpion.label>
  <!--EN: Make large passive coolers, a way to cool indoor spaces below freezing point without needing electricity, or hot stones, a primitive heater.-->
  <VFEC_TemperatureControl.description>制作大型被动式冷却器，一种无需电力即可将室内空间冷却到冰点以下的方法，或制作热石头，一种原始的加热器。</VFEC_TemperatureControl.description>
  <VFEC_TemperatureControl.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->masters of elements-->
    <li>subject-&gt;元素大师</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->harnessed natural methods to defy the whims of weather, creating spaces of comfort through passive coolers and hot stones-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;利用自然方法来对抗天气的变化，通过被动冷却器和 性感的 石头创造舒适的空间</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->cultivating havens of warmth and coolness, in defiance of the external world-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;无视外部世界，培育温暖和凉爽的避风港</li>
  </VFEC_TemperatureControl.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: temperature control-->
  <VFEC_TemperatureControl.label>温度控制</VFEC_TemperatureControl.label>
  <!--EN: Construct large thermaebath that uses steam geysers to warm up the water, allowing up to 8 people to bathe together with an occasional chance of group lovin’.-->
  <VFEC_Thermaebath.description>建造大型温泉浴场，使用蒸汽间歇泉加热水，最多可容纳 8 人一起沐浴，偶尔还有集体爱的机会。</VFEC_Thermaebath.description>
  <VFEC_Thermaebath.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->sanctuaries of steam-->
    <li>subject-&gt;蒸汽圣地</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->constructed thermaebaths, communal havens of relaxation and warmth powered by the earth's breath-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;建造了温泉浴场，这是由大地呼吸提供动力的放松和温暖的公共避风港</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->fostering communal well-being and intimacy in the embrace of nature's warmth-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;在大自然温暖的怀抱中促进社区福祉和亲密</li>
  </VFEC_Thermaebath.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: thermaebath-->
  <VFEC_Thermaebath.label>温泉浴</VFEC_Thermaebath.label>
  <!--EN: Craft togas, everyday wear of the citizens of the republic.-->
  <VFEC_Togas.description>工艺长袍，共和国公民的日常服装。</VFEC_Togas.description>
  <VFEC_Togas.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the fabric of society-->
    <li>subject-&gt;社会结构</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->reclaimed the elegance and simplicity of the toga, the symbol of citizenship and refined taste-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;恢复了托加袍的优雅和简约，它是公民身份和高雅品味的象征</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->draping the republic in the dignity and grace of its ancestors-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;为共和国披上祖先的尊严和优雅</li>
  </VFEC_Togas.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: togas-->
  <VFEC_Togas.label>礼服</VFEC_Togas.label>
  <!--EN: Create a tyrian farm - a river-bank structure that dyes cloth, which can then be extracted in the form of extremely valuable royal fabric.-->
  <VFEC_TyrianProduction.description>创建一个泰尔农场 - 一个河岸结构，用于染色布料，然后可以以极其有价值的皇家织物的形式提取。</VFEC_TyrianProduction.description>
  <VFEC_TyrianProduction.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->the hue of royalty-->
    <li>subject-&gt;皇室色调</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->cultivated tyrian farms along the riverbanks, mastering the art of dyeing cloth into royal fabric, a symbol of wealth and status-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;沿着河岸开垦泰尔农场，掌握将布料染成皇家织物的艺术，这是财富和地位的象征</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->weaving the fabric of society with colors that command respect and admiration-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;用值得尊重和钦佩的颜色编织社会结构</li>
  </VFEC_TyrianProduction.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: tyrian production-->
  <VFEC_TyrianProduction.label>泰尔生产</VFEC_TyrianProduction.label>
  <!--EN: Build a huge, wood-fired stone crematorium which vaporizes corpses with high temperatures.-->
  <VFEC_WoodfiredCrematorium.description>建造一个巨大的燃木石头火葬场，用高温蒸发尸体。</VFEC_WoodfiredCrematorium.description>
  <VFEC_WoodfiredCrematorium.generalRules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: subject->purification by flame-->
    <li>subject-&gt;火焰净化</li>
    <!--EN: subject_story->conceived the wood-fired crematorium, a testament to dealing with the departed in a manner that respects both cultural customs and sanitation needs-->
    <li>subject_story-&gt;构思了燃木火葬场，证明以尊重文化习俗和卫生需求的方式处理死者</li>
    <!--EN: subject_gerund->embracing the cycle of life and death through the elemental purity of fire-->
    <li>subject_gerund-&gt;通过火的元素纯度拥抱生与死的循环</li>
  </VFEC_WoodfiredCrematorium.generalRules.rulesStrings>
  <!--EN: wood-fired crematorium-->
  <VFEC_WoodfiredCrematorium.label>燃木火葬场</VFEC_WoodfiredCrematorium.label>
</LanguageData>
